{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-explainer-about-everyday-conversations-in-real-places-in-america-and-europe-show-what-p/audio/main-012b311c99ff.mp3","durationSec":295.56,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.92,"text":"Small talk is short, friendly talk about light things, like the weather."},{"start":4.64,"end":7.16,"text":"In New York City, a lot of it happens on the move."},{"start":7.74,"end":12.88,"text":"The New York City Subway carries millions of riders every day, and the cars are often crowded."},{"start":13.48,"end":16.52,"text":"People stand close, but most stay quiet with strangers."},{"start":17.24,"end":20.6,"text":"When they do speak, the pace is fast and the topic is practical."},{"start":21.24,"end":25.34,"text":"A rider asks which train stops at a station, or mentions another delay."},{"start":26.16,"end":31.28,"text":"Weather comes up, but in a useful way: it is raining, so the walk from the station will be wet."},{"start":32.22,"end":36.16,"text":"Here is the lens for the whole lesson: place, pace, and topic."},{"start":37.26,"end":42.66,"text":"On the subway, the place is tight, the pace is quick, and the topic is getting somewhere."},{"start":43.5,"end":46.58,"text":"A morning train in Tokyo feels similar in that way."},{"start":47.32,"end":50.66,"text":"In London, people wait in queues, and a queue is a line."},{"start":51.3,"end":55.06,"text":"The queue is orderly, and standing in it is a shared moment."},{"start":55.48,"end":57.38,"text":"This is where small talk fits well."},{"start":58,"end":62.12,"text":"The place is calm, the pace is medium, and the topic is often the weather."},{"start":62.9,"end":68.38,"text":"Someone mentions that it is cold today, and the next person agrees and adds that it may rain later."},{"start":69.18,"end":74.68,"text":"These are short turns, a sentence or two each, and then the talk stops when the coffee arrives."},{"start":75.92,"end":83.3,"text":"Politeness matters in United Kingdom culture, so people use please, thank you, and sorry often, even in a two-line chat."},{"start":84.24,"end":89.46,"text":"Coffee culture is social in many countries, but the London queue version is light and quick."},{"start":89.98,"end":93.34,"text":"It feels warmer than the subway car because nobody is rushing to a door."},{"start":93.34,"end":98.9,"text":"Madrid is the capital of Spain, and much of its social life happens outdoors in the evening."},{"start":99.82,"end":105.16,"text":"Plaza Mayor is a big historic square in the center of Madrid, and it works as a public meeting place."},{"start":106,"end":109.34,"text":"Smaller neighborhood plazas do the same job for the people who live nearby."},{"start":110,"end":110.94,"text":"Now apply the lens."},{"start":111.52,"end":116.02,"text":"The place is open and shared, the pace is slow, and the topic is people."},{"start":116.68,"end":119.98,"text":"Friends and families sit outside, and the talk lasts an hour or more."},{"start":120.56,"end":125.3,"text":"Food is a natural topic: what to eat tonight, and which bar has good snacks."},{"start":126.16,"end":129.44,"text":"Weekend plans come up, and so do family news and children."},{"start":130.26,"end":132.12,"text":"This is the opposite end from the subway."},{"start":133,"end":136.28,"text":"Nobody is going anywhere, so the talk can grow long and relaxed."},{"start":137.12,"end":141.54,"text":"Berlin is the capital of Germany, and it is a working city with a normal workday rhythm."},{"start":142.24,"end":145.28,"text":"The office kitchen is where short workday talk happens."},{"start":147.75,"end":151.63,"text":"People come in for coffee, and that gives them a reason to stand together for a minute."},{"start":151.63,"end":158.29,"text":"Conversation norms in Germany are direct and practical, so the talk is clear and to the point."},{"start":158.87,"end":162.71,"text":"Someone asks about the meeting at ten, or mentions that the project is behind."},{"start":163.69,"end":167.87,"text":"Weekend plans appear on Friday: a trip, a birthday, or just rest."},{"start":168.53,"end":174.69,"text":"Weather is fine as a topic, but it usually leads to a plan, like taking the bike if it stays dry."},{"start":175.75,"end":181.17,"text":"Under the lens, the place is a work space, the pace is quick, and the topic is the day."},{"start":181.81,"end":183.35,"text":"The talk ends when the cup is full."},{"start":184.65,"end":188.55,"text":"Paris is the capital of France, and its mornings often start at a bakery."},{"start":189.63,"end":195.11,"text":"A bakery is a shop that sells bread and pastries, and in the morning a line forms outside."},{"start":196.01,"end":200.63,"text":"The place is busy, the pace is quick, and the topic is food first."},{"start":201.71,"end":207.69,"text":"People name the bread they want, and they comment on the croissants being fresh or the good ones being gone."},{"start":208.79,"end":215.17,"text":"Talk with a neighbor in line is a short turn, often about morning plans: work, school, or a visit."},{"start":215.55,"end":220.91,"text":"The bakery line is like the London queue in shape, but the topic moves from weather to bread."},{"start":221.71,"end":227.33,"text":"In Japan, a quick word at a station bakery or a convenience store counter plays a similar role."},{"start":227.91,"end":230.49,"text":"It is talk that fits between two other tasks."},{"start":231.11,"end":236.11,"text":"This lesson looks at everyday conversations in real places in America with clear city examples."},{"start":236.11,"end":240.07,"text":"Cities in Europe give more examples of the same daily talk."},{"start":240.73,"end":243.31,"text":"These chats happen in named settings that learners can picture."},{"start":244.19,"end":247.55,"text":"This shows how talk differs by place while needs stay familiar."},{"start":248.29,"end":250.49,"text":"Put the five places side by side with the lens."},{"start":251.23,"end":256.75,"text":"The human needs are the same everywhere: weather, food, work or school, and weekend plans."},{"start":257.69,"end":260.55,"text":"The place changes what comes first and how long it lasts."},{"start":261.49,"end":266.03,"text":"On the New York City subway, weather is about a wet walk, and the talk lasts seconds."},{"start":266.99,"end":271.49,"text":"In a London cafe queue, weather is the polite opening, and the talk lasts a minute."},{"start":272.25,"end":275.01,"text":"In a Madrid plaza, food and family fill an evening."},{"start":275.77,"end":279.17,"text":"In a Berlin office kitchen, work and coffee fill a short break."},{"start":279.71,"end":282.71,"text":"In a Paris bakery line, bread fills the moment."},{"start":282.71,"end":286.87,"text":"Fast, tight, task places make short practical talk."},{"start":287.85,"end":291.25,"text":"Slow, open, social places make long personal talk."},{"start":292.05,"end":295.05,"text":"If you know the place and the pace, you can guess the topic."}],"words":[{"text":"Small","start":0,"end":0.28},{"text":"talk","start":0.28,"end":0.58},{"text":"is","start":0.58,"end":0.88},{"text":"short","start":0.88,"end":1.28},{"text":"friendly","start":1.28,"end":1.94},{"text":"talk","start":1.94,"end":2.24},{"text":"about","start":2.24,"end":2.5},{"text":"light","start":2.5,"end":2.74},{"text":"things","start":2.74,"end":3.14},{"text":"like","start":3.4,"end":3.52},{"text":"the","start":3.52,"end":3.66},{"text":"weather","start":3.66,"end":3.92},{"text":"In","start":4.64,"end":4.76},{"text":"New","start":4.76,"end":4.92},{"text":"York","start":4.92,"end":5.1},{"text":"City","start":5.1,"end":5.42},{"text":"a","start":5.72,"end":5.86},{"text":"lot","start":5.86,"end":6.04},{"text":"of","start":6.04,"end":6.16},{"text":"it","start":6.16,"end":6.26},{"text":"happens","start":6.26,"end":6.54},{"text":"on","start":6.54,"end":6.76},{"text":"the","start":6.76,"end":6.88},{"text":"move","start":6.88,"end":7.16},{"text":"The","start":7.74,"end":7.84},{"text":"